---
import ProjectLayout from '../../layouts/ProjectLayout.astro';
---

<ProjectLayout
	title="Chalk & Table"
	description="A full-stack pool league management platform built to handle the complexities of running a real league."
>
<section class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 pb-20 pt-16 lg:px-10 lg:pb-28 lg:pt-24">
		<div class="max-w-4xl">
			<p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-orange-700">
				POOL LEAGUE MANAGEMENT PLATFORM · 2026
			</p>

			<h1 class="mt-5 font-serif text-6xl leading-none tracking-tight text-mist-950 lg:text-8xl">
				Chalk & Table
			</h1>

			<p class="mt-8 max-w-3xl font-serif text-2xl italic leading-relaxed text-mist-600 lg:text-3xl">
				From opening break to the championship match.
			</p>

			<p class="mt-8 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-8 text-mist-700">
				A full-stack pool league management platform built to handle the complexities of running a real league: 
                teams, seasons, scheduling, player rosters, match results, standings, and playoffs.
			</p>

			<div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-3 text-sm text-mist-600">
				<span>Next.js</span>
				<span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
				<span>TypeScript</span>
				<span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
				<span>PostgreSQL</span>
				<span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
				<span>Tailwind CSS</span>
				<span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
				<span>AWS</span>
			</div>

			<div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap gap-4">
				<a
					href="https://chalkandtable.brianrhackett.com"
					target="_blank"
					rel="noopener noreferrer"
					class="rounded-full bg-mist-950 px-6 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-taupe-100 transition hover:bg-mist-800"
				>
					View live ↗
				</a>

				<a
					href="https://github.com/brianrhackett/chalkandtable"
					target="_blank"
					rel="noopener noreferrer"
					class="rounded-full border border-mist-800 px-6 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-mist-950 transition hover:bg-mist-950 hover:text-taupe-100"
				>
					GitHub ↗
				</a>
			</div>
		</div>

		<div class="mt-16 overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-taupe-300">
			<img
				src="/images/projects/ct-league_dashboard.png"
				alt="AgencyOS dashboard showing projects, tasks, milestones, and agency activity"
				class="block h-auto w-full"
			/>
		</div>
	</section>

    <section class="bg-taupe-900 text-mist-100 pb-20 pt-16 lg:pb-28 lg:pt-24">
        <div class="text-lg lg:text-xl mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 lg:px-10">
            <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-6xl font-serif lg:mr-[60%] uppercase">
                The Project
                <span class="text-orange-700 normal-case block font-sans mt-6 text-sm md:text-lg">
                    Built around the way real pool leagues work.
                </span>
            </h2>
            <div class="md:ml-[25%] lg:ml-[40%]">
                <p class="my-6">
                    Chalk & Table began with a simple idea: build a league management platform that 
                    reflects how local pool leagues actually operate.
                </p>
                <p class="my-6">
                    As a member of a local pool league, I was familiar with the challenges of organizing teams, 
                    managing schedules, tracking results, and keeping standings up to date. 
                    What seemed like a straightforward application quickly revealed a surprising amount of complexity.
                </p>
                <p class="my-6">
                    Teams share venues, schedules need to account for holidays and other conflicts, 
                    seasons follow different formats, and playoff structures introduce their own rules. 
                    Rather than building around a rigid set of assumptions, I wanted to create something flexible 
                    enough to accommodate different leagues.
                </p>
                <p class="my-6">
                    The result is a full-stack application that brings league administration, scheduling, team rosters, 
                    match results, player statistics, standings, and playoffs together in one place.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 pb-20 pt-16 lg:px-10 lg:pb-28 lg:pt-24 text-lg lg:text-xl">
        <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-6xl font-serif lg:ml-[60%] uppercase">
            League Management
            <span class="text-orange-700 normal-case block font-sans mt-6 text-sm md:text-lg">
                Every team, every season, all in one place.
            </span>
        </h2>
        <div class="mr:ml-[25%] lg:mr-[40%]">
            <p class="my-6">
                Chalk &amp; Table organizes each league into seasons, allowing administrators to manage teams, 
                venues, and player rosters while preserving results from previous years.
            </p>
            <p class="my-6">
                Teams can be assigned to shared venues, players can be added to seasonal rosters, and captains 
                can be designated to help manage their teams. Each season maintains its own schedule, 
                standings, and results, providing a complete picture of league activity.
            </p>
            <p class="my-6">
                Standings are calculated automatically from completed matches, tracking wins, losses, 
                and rack percentages to give teams an up-to-date view of their performance throughout the season.
            </p>
        </div>
        <div class="grid gap-6 lg:gap-10 grid-cols-1 md-gridcols-2 my-20">
            <div>
                <img
                    src='/images/projects/ct-rosters_section.png'
                    alt="roster section of team page"
                    class="w-full"
                />
                <p class="my-6 text-sm px-6 text-center">
                    Teams can opt-in to keep track of individual rack statistics throughout a season. This will keep track
                    of each player's individual win/loss record.
                </p>
            </div>
            <div>
                <img
                    src='/images/projects/ct-standings.png'
                    alt="Standings page"
                    class="w-full"
                />
                <p class="my-6 text-sm px-6 text-center">
                    Standings are calculated automatically based on match results. Tiebreakers are built-in which include 
                    head-to-head records and total racks won, as well as a "mini league table" calculation when more than
                    two teams are tied.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="bg-taupe-900 text-mist-100 pb-20 pt-16 lg:pb-28 lg:pt-24">
        <div class="text-lg lg:text-xl mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 lg:px-10">
            <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-6xl font-serif lg:mr-[60%] uppercase">
                Scheduling
                <span class="text-orange-700 normal-case block font-sans mt-6 text-sm md:text-lg">
                    More than just putting dates on a calendar.
                </span>
            </h2>
            <div class="md:ml-[25%] lg:ml-[40%]">
                <p class="my-6">
                    Generating a league schedule involves more than pairing teams together. 
                    Matches need to be distributed fairly, home and away assignments need to be balanced, 
                    and teams sharing the same venue can't be scheduled at home simultaneously.
                </p>
                <p class="my-6">
                    Chalk & Table includes a schedule generator that handles round-robin competition 
                    while accounting for these constraints. Administrators can choose the day of the week, 
                    exclude holidays or other unavailable dates, and select the season's scheduling format.
                </p>
                <p class="my-6">
                    Before committing anything to the database, the generated schedule can be previewed 
                    and reviewed. For leagues with an existing schedule, a CSV import option provides an 
                    alternative to automatic generation.
                </p>
            </div>
            <div class="grid gap-6 lg:gap-10 grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 mt-10">
                <div>
                    <img 
                        src='/images/projects/ct-schedule_format.png'
                        alt="Options for format of schedule"
                    />
                    <div class="text-center text-sm text-orange-700 mt-2">
                        <div class="uppercase">Schedule Format</div>
                        Choose between single round-robin, home-and-away, or a fixed number of weeks.
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <img 
                        src='/images/projects/ct-schedule_options.png'
                        alt="View of all options chosen"
                    />
                    <div class="text-center text-sm text-orange-700 mt-2">
                        <div class="uppercase">Schedule Confirmation</div>
                        Review scheduling options before generating and approving the final schedule.
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 pb-20 pt-16 lg:px-10 lg:pb-28 lg:pt-24 text-lg lg:text-xl">
        <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-6xl font-serif lg:ml-[60%] uppercase mb-12">
            Match Management
            <span class="text-orange-700 normal-case block font-sans mt-6 text-sm md:text-lg">
                From the opening break to the final rack.
            </span>
        </h2>
        <div class="md:ml-[25%] lg:ml-[40%]">
            <p class="my-6">
                Chalk & Table provides a dedicated match page where teams can manage lineups, record results, 
                and track individual player performance throughout the season.
            </p>
            <p class="my-6">
                Team captains can select players from their seasonal rosters to build match lineups, 
                while authorized users can enter final scores and record rack-by-rack results. 
                Completed matches are locked to prevent accidental changes to recorded results.
            </p>
            <p class="my-6">
                For leagues that enable individual player statistics, rack results are used to calculate each 
                player's wins and losses automatically. This allows leagues to track individual performance 
                without requiring a separate scorekeeping system.
            </p>
            <p class="my-6">
                Match results also feed directly into the league standings, keeping team records and rankings 
                up to date as the season progresses.
            </p>
        </div>
        <div class="grid gap-6 lg:gap-10 grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 mt-10">
            <div>
                <img 
                    src='/images/projects/ct-weekly_schedule.png'
                    alt="Weekly schedule overview"
                />
                <div class="text-center text-sm text-orange-700 mt-2">
                    <div class="uppercase">Weekly Schedules</div>
                    Schedule page is broken down by weeks.
                </div>
            </div>
            <div>
                <img 
                    src='/images/projects/ct-add_score.png'
                    alt="View of score editing"
                />
                <div class="text-center text-sm text-orange-700 mt-2">
                    <div class="uppercase">Score Entering</div>
                    A simple modal interface for entering match scores.
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="bg-taupe-900 text-mist-100 pb-20 pt-16 lg:pb-28 lg:pt-24">
        <div class="text-lg lg:text-xl mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 lg:px-10">
            <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-6xl font-serif lg:mr-[60%] uppercase">
                Playoffs
                <span class="text-orange-700 normal-case block font-sans mt-6 text-sm md:text-lg">
                    The road to the championship.
                </span>
            </h2>
            <div class="md:ml-[25%] lg:ml-[40%]">
                <p class="my-6">
                    The regular season is only part of the story. Chalk & Table also supports configurable
                    playoff tournaments, allowing leagues to define their postseason structure rather than 
                    being locked into a single format.
                </p>
                <p class="my-6">
                    Administrators can configure playoff rounds, determine how many teams qualify, and 
                    establish the number of matches required to win each series. The system supports different 
                    formats for each round, including best-of-three and best-of-five series.
                </p>
                <p class="my-6">
                    As results are recorded, teams advance through the tournament bracket, with support for 
                    reseeding between rounds. The bracket provides a clear view of each matchup, series results, 
                    and the path to the championship.
                </p>
                <p class="my-6">
                    By integrating playoffs with the existing teams, rosters, and match management system, 
                    Chalk & Table keeps the postseason connected to the rest of the league.
                </p>
            </div>
            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 mt-10">
                <div>
                    <img 
                        src='/images/projects/ct-playoffs.png'
                        alt="Playoff bracket with champion"
                    />
                    <div class="text-center text-sm text-orange-700 mt-2">
                        <div class="uppercase">Playoff Bracket</div>
                        Complete playoff bracket with championship call-out.
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 pb-20 pt-16 lg:px-10 lg:pb-28 lg:pt-24 text-lg lg:text-xl">
        <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-6xl font-serif lg:ml-[60%] uppercase mb-12">
            Under The Hood
            <span class="text-orange-700 normal-case block font-sans mt-6 text-sm md:text-lg">
                Built with Next.js. Designed for the complexities of real league management.
            </span>
        </h2>
        <div class="grid gap-6 lg:gap-10 grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2">
            <div>
                <h3 class="text-sm text-mist-600 tracking uppercase">
                    Next.js + React
                </h3>
                <p class="mt-6 text-lg">
                    Full-stack application built with Next.js 16, React, and TypeScript, using 
                    server components, server actions, and interactive client components.
                </p>
            </div>
            <div>
                <h3 class="text-sm text-mist-600 tracking uppercase">
                    PostGreSQL + Prisma
                </h3>
                <p class="mt-6 text-lg">
                    Relational database modeling leagues, seasons, teams, venues, players, matches, 
                    individual rack results, and playoff series, managed through Prisma ORM.
                 </p>
            </div>
            <div>
                <h3 class="text-sm text-mist-600 tracking uppercase">
                    Authentication &amp; Authorization
                </h3>
                <p class="mt-6 text-lg">
                    Auth.js handles user authentication, while league memberships and role-based 
                    permissions control access to administrative features, team management, and scorekeeping.
                </p>
            </div>
            <div>
                <h3 class="text-sm text-mist-600 tracking uppercase">
                    Scheduling &amp; Tournament Logic
                </h3>
                <p class="mt-6 text-lg">
                    Custom round-robin scheduling algorithms account for shared venues, home-and-away 
                    assignments, and excluded dates. Configurable playoff structures manage tournament 
                    series and progression.
                </p>
            </div>
            <div>
                <h3 class="text-sm text-mist-600 tracking uppercase">
                    Tailwind CSS
                </h3>
                <p class="mt-6 text-lg">
                    Responsive interfaces built with Tailwind CSS, including customizable league themes, 
                    interactive scheduling tools, match scorekeeping, and tournament brackets.
                </p>
            </div>
            <div>
                <h3 class="text-sm text-mist-600 tracking uppercase">
                    AWS + Nginx
                </h3>
                <p class="mt-6 text-lg">
                    Deployed on Amazon EC2 with Nginx, PostgreSQL, and PM2 managing the production Next.js application.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="bg-taupe-900 text-mist-100 pb-20 pt-16 lg:pb-28 lg:pt-24">
        <div class="text-lg lg:text-xl mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 lg:px-10">
            <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-6xl font-serif lg:mr-[60%] uppercase">
                Building Chalk & Table
                <span class="text-orange-700 normal-case block font-sans mt-6 text-sm md:text-lg">
                    What started as a league manager became something much bigger.
                </span>
            </h2>
            <div class="md:ml-[25%] lg:ml-[40%]">
                <p class="my-6">
                    Chalk & Table began as an opportunity to build a practical application around 
                    something I already knew well. Having played in a local pool league, I understood how the league operated, 
                    but translating those rules and routines into software presented an entirely different set of challenges.
                </p>
                <p class="my-6">
                    What initially seemed like a straightforward combination of teams, schedules, and standings 
                    grew into a much more complex system. Supporting multiple seasons, shared venues, 
                    configurable playoff formats, player statistics, and different levels of user access required 
                    careful consideration of how each part of the application interacted with the others.
                </p>
                <p class="my-6">
                    Some of the most rewarding challenges involved the logic behind the scenes. Building a schedule generator 
                    that accounted for venue conflicts and balanced home-and-away assignments, designing a playoff system flexible 
                    enough to accommodate different tournament formats, and maintaining consistent permissions across the 
                    application all pushed me beyond simply creating pages and database records.
                </p>
                <p class="my-6">
                    Developing Chalk & Table strengthened my experience with Next.js, TypeScript, relational data modeling, 
                    and full-stack application architecture. More importantly, it reinforced the value of understanding 
                    the problem before designing the solution, and of building software that can adapt as real-world 
                    requirements evolve.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="bg-taupe-100">
        <div class="mx-auto flex max-w-7xl justify-end px-6 py-20 lg:px-10 lg:py-24">
            <div class="w-full max-w-sm text-right md:text-left">
                <p class="font-serif text-3xl italic text-mist-500">
                    Next Project
                </p>

                <a
                    href="/projects/agencyos"
                    class="mt-5 inline-block text-lg font-medium text-orange-700 transition hover:text-orange-800"
                >
                    AgencyOS &rarr;
                </a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

</ProjectLayout>